      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAn AMD monokernel launch (`--enable-amd-monokernel`, sgl-amd-mono) keeps all of its workgroups resident and waiting on each other through device-memory flags. The overlap scheduler issues small kernels on its own `schedule_stream`, and the result readback runs on `copy_stream`. If one of those kernels takes a CU while a monokernel launch is being dispatched, some of the launch's workgroups cannot become resident. The resident ones then wait until the plugin's guard deadline (60 s) stops every rank, and the log shows a GPU memory fault at address `(nil)`.\n\nOn Muse Spark TP8 with the monokernels on 8x MI355X, this hit about once every 15-60 min at concurrency 1 and 4 on the full AgentX trace set, always in the DFlash2 draft's first launch. A standalone repro replays that launch's CUDA graph and runs one small kernel every 100 ms on a second stream: 4 of 8 GPUs hang within 7 min. The same replays without the second stream ran 200M launches clean.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py`: with `--enable-amd-monokernel`, `schedule_stream` and `copy_stream` are the forward stream. The host side still overlaps; only the scheduler's GPU work queues behind the forward. Nothing changes without the flag.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nNA (no numerics change).\n\n## Benchmark\n\nMuse Spark Open TP8 + monokernels, 8x MI355X, InferenceX AgentX full trace set, 3600 s: concurrency 1 and 4 now run clean with no hang, at the same speed as before the change. The InferenceX sweep in [InferenceX #4606](https://github.com/SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX/pull/4606) (`lmsysorg/sglang-rocm:muse-spark-open-1027`) carries this change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41560513200](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41560513200)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41560513146](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41560513146)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41560513130](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41560513130)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
